15. Rfd1 Qc7 16. Na5 Bc6 17. Nc4 Bb5 18. Nxb5 axb5 19. Ra7 Qd8 20. Bb6 Qe8 21.
Nxd6 Bxd6 22. Qxd6 Rxc2 23. Qd3 Qc6 24. Be3 {JS notes: Open Swiss: (1)
Jonathan Century 6/7; (2-3) A Kanamori, John Nunn 5.5; (4-5) PJ Booth, Graham
P Burton 5; (6-11) James M Aitken, G Bromley, Mike J Conroy, David A Hester,
John M Ripley, Kevin J Wicker 4.5. I (JS) was amongst those on 4. 46
competitors (BCM, Sept 1971, p329) The main event was a 14-player, 9-round
Swiss: (1) G Botterill 6.5/9; (2) V Ciocaltea 6; (3) Peter Markland 5.5; (4-7)
J Eslon, RR Smith, Andrew Whiteley, Danny Wright 5, etc. There was also a
women's tournament won by E Polihroniade 6.5, Jana Hartston 5.5, etc.  TH
notes: My first tournament after an almost complete 18 month break from chess.
The congress organiser was Alan K. Crombleholme. One of the titled players in
the master section whom Botterill defeated was Gliksman.} 1/2-1/2

